TA-gen_ai_cim - bin/ scripts
=============================

The Python shipped with the add-on. Every script runs under Splunk's bundled
interpreter (python.required = 3.13 on Splunk 9.4+, Python 3.9 on older
releases), uses only the standard library plus the vendored lib/splunklib, and
compiles on both. Loggers are module-level and write under
$SPLUNK_HOME/var/log/splunk/. No script logs a credential or puts one in a URL.

Custom search commands (default/commands.conf)
----------------------------------------------

aicase.py
    `| aicase` - creates or looks up ServiceNow AI Case records linked to
    GenAI events.

genaiscore.py
    `| genaiscore pipeline=<name>` - enriches events with LLM-derived risk
    scores through Splunk AI Toolkit's Connection Management.

genaiseedes.py (over genai_es_seed.py)
    `| genaiseedes` - seeds the TA-owned Mission Control records (response
    plans, the AI Findings queue) and binds plan tasks to the paired SOAR.
    Run hourly and on startup by "GenAI - ES - Seed Response Plan and SOAR
    Binding".

Alert actions (default/alert_actions.conf)
------------------------------------------

create_snow_case.py      create_snow_aicase - opens a ServiceNow AI Case.
sync_snow_asset.py       sync_snow_asset - reconciles AI systems and models
                         with the ServiceNow inventory tables. It also holds
                         the shared ServiceNow client (get_snow_config, OAuth,
                         HTTP) every ServiceNow consumer imports.
pull_snow_inventory.py   pull_snow_inventory - pulls the full ServiceNow AI
                         inventory into KV store (an alert action, not an
                         input).
ai_defense_*.py          Simulated containment actions over
                         ai_defense_response.py; every record they write
                         carries "simulated": true.

Modular input (README/inputs.conf.spec)
---------------------------------------

ta_gen_ai_cim_duo.py
    The entry point Splunk runs for scheme ta_gen_ai_cim_duo (Splunk resolves
    a scheme to bin/<scheme>.py). A shim that calls
    ta_gen_ai_cim_duo_input.main(); it holds no logic.

ta_gen_ai_cim_duo_input.py
    Scheme ta_gen_ai_cim_duo. Each instance polls one Cisco Duo Admin API
    endpoint (endpoint = authentication, activity or users) with the Duo
    account named in account = <name>, and checkpoints to the
    ta_gen_ai_cim_duo_checkpoint KV collection. Events are
    ta_gen_ai_cim:duo:authentication, :activity and :user. Only the scheme's
    default stanza ships; there is no instance until one is added in local/.
    Reads the duo_hmac account's secret key from storage/passwords with the
    input's own session key.

ta_gen_ai_cim_duo_api.py
    The read-only Duo Admin API client the input uses (v5 HMAC-SHA512
    signing, TLS verified, 20 s timeout, next_offset / offset paging, HTTP
    429 / code 42901 raised as DuoRateLimited, HTTP 5xx or an unreachable Duo
    as DuoUnavailable). Standard library only; never logs a key, a signature,
    an Authorization header or a rejected account url.

REST handler (default/restmap.conf)
-----------------------------------

ta_gen_ai_cim_account_handler.py
    The admin_external handler for ta_gen_ai_cim_account.conf, at
    /servicesNS/nobody/TA-gen_ai_cim/ta_gen_ai_cim_account/ta_gen_ai_cim_account.
    auth_type basic / oauth_auth_code / oauth_client_creds (ServiceNow),
    token (the soar account) and duo_hmac (Cisco Duo Admin API: url is the
    validated https://api-<id>.duosecurity.com or .duofederal.com hostname,
    client_id the integration key). Non-secret settings go to the conf;
    passwords, client secrets, the SOAR token and the Duo secret key go only
    to storage/passwords. List never returns a secret. Create refuses an
    existing name, edit refuses a switch between duo_hmac and another auth
    type, and an empty or masked secret on edit keeps the stored one. The
    Configuration page's Cisco Duo tab saves through it; its ServiceNow tab
    writes configs/conf-ta_gen_ai_cim_account and storage/passwords directly.

Setup helper
------------

snow_setup.py
    CLI that creates or updates a ServiceNow basic-auth account through the
    account REST handler
    (/servicesNS/nobody/TA-gen_ai_cim/ta_gen_ai_cim_account/ta_gen_ai_cim_account).

Accounts and secrets
--------------------

Every secret lives under realm ta_gen_ai_cim_account__<account>, credential
name password or client_secret, in the TA-gen_ai_cim app context. Since
v1.9.0 metadata/default.meta [passwords] limits them to admin and sc_admin
(export = none), and every reader below runs as a role that passes.

    Realm (account)       Read by                         Runs as
    ServiceNow account    sync_snow_asset,                the alert's session_key:
                          pull_snow_inventory             the search owner, admin
                                                          for the five shipped
                                                          ServiceNow searches
                          create_snow_aicase (ad hoc),    the invoking user
                          | aicase
    soar                  | genaiseedes, only with         admin (the shipped
                          install_simulator = true        search is owner = admin)
    Cisco Duo account     the Duo modular input           splunk-system-user (the
                                                          input's own session)

The ServiceNow consumers pick their account with
sync_snow_asset.select_snow_account: the first account by name whose url is
a *.service-now.com or *.servicenow.com host, else the first by name with a
ServiceNow auth_type that is not named soar or duo. A Cisco Duo or soar
account is never used as the ServiceNow account, whatever its name sorts as.

passauth
--------

No command sets passauth: Splunk ignores it for chunked (protocol v2)
commands. Each runs under the invoking session (searchinfo.session_key).
Access is gated by the command ACLs in metadata/default.meta ([commands/aicase]
admin, sc_admin, power; [commands/genaiscore] and [commands/genaiseedes]
admin, sc_admin) and by the ACLs on the confs and credentials each reads; the
shipped scheduled searches that call genaiscore and genaiseedes are owned by
admin. The commands do not execute user input as code, do not shell out, and
write no files outside $SPLUNK_HOME/var/log/splunk/.
